  "instance_name": "historical_event_paris_commune",
  "label": "Paris Commune",
  "description": "The Paris Commune was a revolutionary government that ruled Paris from March 18 to May 28, 1871. It was established after the Franco-Prussian War and is often depicted in historical illustrations as a period of intense social upheaval and violence, including street fighting and mob actions. The bottom image from 'Le Petit Journal Illustré' is a well-known depiction of the Commune's violence, specifically the suppression of the uprising by French government forces. This event is not American, but the meme falsely labels it as 'American history,' which is a key misleading element.",
